{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nEvery operator-seeded SSM `SecureString` secret managed by `infra/terraform` persists its\nCLEARTEXT value in the remote terraform state (S3 `rebar-tfstate-896586841071`, key\n`rebar/prod/terraform.tfstate`, SSE-S3 not a CMK). The `value = \"CHANGEME\"` +\n`lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }` pattern stops terraform WRITING the secret from git, but\nterraform still READS the live value into `attributes.value` on every refresh/import, so the\nplaintext lands in state. This collapses the secret tier to the state-bucket ACL (`terraform state\npull` renders 23 secrets in cleartext to any state-bucket reader), and versioning retains the tail\nacross rotation. Root cause is proven; see the evidence comments below.\n\n## Decision (operator-approved — Option 1)\n\nMigrate every operator-seeded SSM `SecureString` SECRET from the `value = \"CHANGEME\"` +\n`ignore_changes = [value]` pattern to terraform WRITE-ONLY arguments `value_wo` + `value_wo_version`.\nWrite-only arguments are, by design, NEVER persisted to state — the structural fix. Non-secret\n`String` config params (`jira-url`, `jira-user`, `jira-project`) and the terraform-GENERATED\n`SecureString` `opcert_origin_guard` (its value is `random_password.opcert_guard.result`, already in\nstate via the random resource + the API-Gateway header, so `value_wo` gives no net benefit) are OUT\nof scope and stay as-is.\n\n## Approach\n\nThree resources carry the seeded-secret antipattern and migrate to `value_wo`/`value_wo_version`\n(drop `value` and the `lifecycle { ignore_changes = [value] }`):\n- `aws_ssm_parameter.rebar_secrets` (for_each, 18 params) — `infra/terraform/ssm.tf:90`\n- `aws_ssm_parameter.opcert_ed25519_key` — `infra/terraform/opcert.tf:52`\n- `aws_ssm_parameter.cookie_signing_secret` — `infra/terraform/auth_sso.tf:39`\n\n`value_wo = \"CHANGEME\"` + `value_wo_version = 1` preserves the create-placeholder + operator-seed +\nno-revert contract (write-only value is only (re)sent when `value_wo_version` changes, and is never\ncompared/stored, so the operator's out-of-band value is never clobbered and `user_data.sh`'s\n`CHANGEME` fail-fast still fires on an unseeded slot). Raise the `versions.tf` floors, which today\nsit below the write-only floors: terraform `required_version` `>= 1.10` → `>= 1.11` (write-only args\nneed 1.11; host is 1.15.8) and AWS provider `~> 5.0` → `~> 5.79` (`value_wo` on `aws_ssm_parameter`\nneeds 5.79; host/lock is 5.100.0). Rationale: write-only args are the provider-native mechanism\npurpose-built for exactly this (keep a secret out of state) — no new dependency, no secrets-manager,\nno KMS CMK, minimal blast radius.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `infra/terraform/ssm.tf`, `infra/terraform/opcert.tf`, `infra/terraform/auth_sso.tf` — migrate the\n  three secret resources to `value_wo`/`value_wo_version`.\n- `infra/terraform/versions.tf` — raise the terraform + AWS-provider floors.\n- `scripts/check_ssm_secret_state.py` (NEW) — hermetic structural guard (no live AWS) that parses\n  `infra/terraform/*.tf`, and for every `aws_ssm_parameter` with `type = \"SecureString\"` flags the\n  persisted-secret antipattern (a quoted string-literal `value` and/or `ignore_changes = [value]`)\n  and requires `value_wo` be paired with `value_wo_version`. Allows the generated-value case\n  (`value` = an expression, no `ignore_changes`). Modeled on `scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py`.\n- `Makefile` — wire the new guard into `make lint` (alongside `check_templatefile_escapes.py` at\n  `Makefile:302`).\n- `tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py` (NEW) — pins RED→GREEN + mutation teeth + committed\n  tree clean + make-lint wiring, mirroring `tests/unit/test_check_templatefile_escapes.py`.\n- `docs/adr/0105-ssm-secrets-never-in-terraform-state.md` (+ `docs/adr/.numbers/0105`, regenerated\n  `docs/adr/README.md`) — record the decision, extending ADR 0008 and relating to ADR 0046.\n- `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` (NEW) — declare/seed/rotate via write-only args, and the\n  operator REMEDIATION procedure (state scrub + crown-jewel rotation).\n\n## Testing\n\n- RED first: the new guard/test fail against the CURRENT tree for the right reason (three\n  SecureString secrets persist a `value` literal + `ignore_changes = [value]`); proven before the\n  fix.\n- GREEN after: guard + test pass once the three resources use `value_wo`/`value_wo_version`.\n- Mutation teeth: reverting any one param to `value = \"…\" + ignore_changes = [value]` returns the\n  guard to RED (asserted by `tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py`).\n- `terraform validate` in `infra/terraform` passes (static; no plan/apply against the real backend —\n  that prod mutation is the deferred operator ticket, linked `discovered_from`).\n- `make lint` passes (ruff + the new guard + siblings).\n\nNo secret VALUE is printed, logged, or committed by the fix or its verification — the guard digests\nstructure only, never values.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] All three seeded-secret `SecureString` resources (`rebar_secrets`, `opcert_ed25519_key`,\n      `cookie_signing_secret`) use `value_wo` + `value_wo_version` and carry no `value`/`ignore_changes\n      = [value]`; verified by `scripts/check_ssm_secret_state.py` exiting 0 and by reading the diff.\n- [ ] `scripts/check_ssm_secret_state.py` is RED on the pre-fix tree and GREEN on the post-fix tree,\n      and a one-param mutation returns it to RED; verified by `tests/unit/test_check_ssm_secret_state.py`.\n- [ ] The guard is wired into `make lint`; verified by a wiring test and by `make lint` exit 0.\n- [ ] `versions.tf` floors are terraform `>= 1.11` and AWS provider `~> 5.79`; verified by reading the file.\n- [ ] `terraform validate` in `infra/terraform` succeeds; verified by its exit 0.\n- [ ] ADR 0105 exists with marker `docs/adr/.numbers/0105`, the index is regenerated, and\n      `scripts/check_adr_numbers.py` + `python scripts/gen_adr_index.py --check` pass.\n- [ ] `infra/runbooks/ssm-secret-write-only.md` covers declare/seed/rotate + the exposure-remediation\n      procedure and cross-links ADR 0105; verified by reading it.\n- [ ] A deferred OPERATOR `task` ticket for the prod remediation (apply → verify no SecureString value\n      in `terraform state pull` → rotate crown-jewels) exists and is linked `discovered_from` this\n      ticket; verified by `show_ticket`. [non-codebase] evidence: the new ticket id recorded in a comment.\n- [ ] No credential value is printed, logged, or committed by the fix or its verification."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788023214164142592,"uuid":"ce806d06-96e5-409c-acba-11f744ba3677"}